m that is a walk-up system  where you can readily generate data in a  short period of time  and because of the the nature of the  data  you can reduce some of the subjectivity  and decisions and bias that come  from running color tests  so it this is a faster screening method  when you compare to color test  and then layer there's you're not  waiting  for anything you're not putting a  sequence  on you're not uh you know doing all of  those things that  by their nature take time and this  variable cone voltage  is you know very good in terms of  it's a much added benefit to be able to  see  specific fragmentation at these  different  code voltages it's easy  minimal training is required so i'm  involved in teaching  an instrumental course for forensic  scientists  we had the system in-house so part of  our mass spec  lesson is i had them  the students run their unknowns they  were given unknowns and they ran it  on the system so they had minimal  training  we just told them here's what you can do  here's what you can't do  and they ran their samples and they got  their results  so because your data acquisition is mass  links  you can actually go back into the data  and do  more interactive analyses we did this  because we were wondering why  we weren't able to find traces of  compound a when compound b was present  and we went into mass lines and we could  see okay well it's there but  uh you know its intensity is much  smaller than  the major component so if you're  comfortable with mass links  you do have the capability of going  further than live id  [Music]  okay so some of the disadvantages are  going to be if you're used to  chromatography if you like that  separation you're not going to get it  with  a system like this so as such  uh because we can't separate compounds  out  um we're not going to be able to  identify  all the components in the single sample  because we don't always know what's in a  sample  sometimes we get carry over so the lab  is going to 